<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cao Shu Zhenduo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cao Shu, Zhenduo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cao Shu Zhenduo was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wen-of-zhou">King Wen of Zhou</a> and younger brother of King Wu, who after the Zhou conquest of Shang in the eleventh century BCE enfeoffed him at Taoqiu, in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>. He became the founder of the ruling house of the State of Cao, which survived until the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> annexed it in 487 BCE.</p></div>
